course: dictionary
lesson: 6832
title: The outcome of a story, a game or a sum
level: primary-5
stars: 0
explain: An outcome is the result of something, what happens in the end. You can often work out its meaning from the words around it. «Imagining the worst possible outcome is called catastrophising.» The word "possible" tells you an outcome is one of several things that could happen, so it must be a result.
explain: Clues can point in different directions. «Worst-case thinking jumps from a small problem to the most terrible outcome; asking "what is most likely?" helps.» Here the outcome is where the problem ends up. The question "what is most likely?" tells you that a good thinker looks for the realistic outcome, not the scariest one.
explain: In maths, an outcome is one possible result of an event. Tossing a coin has 2 outcomes, heads or tails. Check your meaning by swapping in "result": "the most terrible result" still makes sense, so you have understood the word.
fact: An outcome is the result of something, what happens in the end.
fact: In maths probability, an outcome is one possible result of an event, such as heads or tails when you toss a coin.
fact: A coin has 2 outcomes, and a dice has 6 outcomes.
fact: Probability is the number of favourable outcomes divided by all the outcomes.
fact: Useful phrases: «the final outcome», «a good outcome», «possible outcomes».
exercise: «Imagining the worst possible outcome is called catastrophising.» In this sentence, what is an outcome? | A number on a dice | A kind of sport | A type of coin | *The result of something, what happens in the end
exercise: A coin is tossed once. How many outcomes are possible? | *2 | 1 | 4 | 6
exercise: «Worst-case thinking jumps from a small problem to the most terrible outcome; asking "what is most likely?" helps.» What does asking "what is most likely?" help you find? | A dice roll | A longer sentence | The worst result of all | *The realistic result, the one most likely to happen
test: A dice is rolled once. How many outcomes are possible? | 4 | 8 | 12 | *6
test: In «a good outcome», what does outcome mean? | A type of game | A length of time | *The result or ending | A kind of coin
exam: Probability is the number of favourable outcomes divided by what? | The dice | The number of players | One | *All the possible outcomes
